  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: The multiprofile + avgpool + scvi_n200 configuration (config_005) achieved 0.650 accuracy, representing the largest gain so far (~13 pts over single-profile). The encoder comparison (scvi_n200 vs PCA-2000) showed a moderate ~3.5 pt gain, and aggregation strategy (transformer vs avgpool) showed negligible difference. Uncertainty: It remains unknown whether scgpt, a more expressive learned RNA encoder, provides a meaningful improvement over scvi_n200 in the multiprofile regime where the biggest gains are realized. Question: config_008 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_005, isolating the encoder effect (scvi_n200 → scgpt) while holding profile setting and aggregation constant. Why this is the best next experiment: Resolving the encoder question before investing in multimodal fusion is critical—multimodal configurations introduce multiple new variables (image encoder, fusion strategy), and committing to a suboptimal RNA encoder would confound those comparisons. If scgpt substantially outperforms scvi_n200, it redefines the best RNA backbone for all downstream fusion experiments; if not, we confirm scvi_n200 is sufficient and can pivot to testing whether the weak image modality (0.208 alone) adds complementary signal via fusion. This single experiment reduces the most important remaining uncertainty in the RNA representation dimension at minimal cost."
}

